    {
      "name": "stoichiometry_and_rate_forms",
      "description": "Every lowering branch in one network. R3 `2 A -> B`: the factor `A ^ 2` (integer exponent) and A's coefficient -2. R4 `A + B -> 2 A`: A on both sides, net +1, so A's term is the bare rate law. R5 `B -> 1.5 C`: an integer rate literal 3 and a fractional coefficient 1.5. R6 is a source (rate alone), R7 a sink. R8 `A + C -> B + C`: C is a catalyst, net 0, so R8 gives C no term. R9 `3 B -> B`: net -2 with `B ^ 3`. R10 has the reservoir M as a factor; M itself gets no equation. R11 has the literal rate 1, which stays in the tree (`1 * O3`). R12 `C -> 0.25 C`: a fractional net -0.75. R13 `0.5 O3 -> NO`: a fractional exponent. X is in no reaction and gets no equation.",
